  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \nA continuation of the Great Lakes troughing pattern remains \nstrongly favored through at least Monday morning, maintaining \nbelow-seasonal temperatures and featuring multiple passages of \nembedded shortwaves that will support periods of showers and \nthunderstorms through the weekend. Model consensus favors \novernight tonight into Saturday morning for the period \ncontaining the most widespread rain and highest accumulations, \ngenerally along an axis from central OH through northwest PA. \nMean QPF values within this higher axis hover around 0.5\" with a\n20-30% probability for jet enhancement to 24-hour totals above \n1\" (less than 1% probability for greater than 2\"). The long \nduration and limited QPF amounts ensure flooding concerns remain \nvery low.\n\nThe upper troughing pattern shifts eastward early next week \nand brings us a short reprieve from the rainy weather. \nUnfortunately, the it doesn't shift very far and ends up\nsettling over eastern Canada and New England, maintaining an \nactive northwest flow over the upper Ohio Valley. As a result, \nwe could see below seasonal temps and periodic rain chances set \nback up mid to late next week.",
